      "source": [
        "**Q: Compare the models under a clearly stated compute budget. Report performance, parameter counts, training cost, trained samples and limitations.**\n",
        "\n",
        "We compare the two baselines on Apple MPS in run `full_20261118T151309Z_9b5cbcb2`, with the shared 20-epoch budget. Each model therefore sees 900,000 training examples across epochs. The table reports the selected validation checkpoint for each network.\n",
        "\n",
        "| | AlexNet | ResNet-18 |\n",
        "|---|---:|---:|\n",
        "| Parameters | 6,976,842 | 11,173,962 |\n",
        "| Best epoch | 17 | 18 |\n",
        "| Validation accuracy | 83.84% | 85.74% |\n",
        "| Validation loss at best | 0.880 | 0.677 |\n",
        "| Training accuracy at best | 99.78% | 100% |\n",
        "| Wall-clock time | 4.95 min | 12.94 min |\n",
        "\n",
        "ResNet reaches a higher validation accuracy (+1.90 percentage points) with about 1.6x as many parameters, at roughly 2.6x the wall time on this machine. Both fits show overfitting: training accuracy is near-perfect while validation stays in the mid-80% range. The comparison uses one seed and one split, and the official test set is still held out for later final evaluation.\n"
      ]
    },
