      "source": [
        "**Q: What did we change, what did we hold fixed, and what do the curves suggest?**\n",
        "\n",
        "We keep AlexNet, the Task 1 split, seed 2223, the 20-epoch SGD+cosine budget, batch size 64 and no augmentation. One shared baseline (`width_mult=1.0`, `dropout=0.5`, `l2=0`) is reused across groups. Capacity changes only `width_mult` (0.5 / 1.0 / 1.5). L2 changes only weight decay (`0` / `1e-4` / `1e-3`). Dropout changes only the head dropout (`0` / `0.25` / `0.5`).\n",
        "\n",
        "We selected the checkpoints and measured wall time in Mac MPS run `full_20261119T172504Z_309c288e`. For each checkpoint, we measured accuracy and loss on the original 45,000 training images with one CPU pass in `eval()` mode. The validation metrics come from the original evaluation on 5,000 images and are stored in the checkpoint. The curves above show training metrics collected during optimizer updates and validation metrics collected at the end of each epoch. To evaluate an existing run, run the setup and shared function cells, then call `evaluate_best_checkpoints` with the run directory.\n",
        "\n",
        "| Run | Params | Best ep | Val acc | Val loss | Train acc (eval) | Train loss (eval) | Acc gap (pp) | Wall |\n",
        "|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|\n",
        "| w0.5 | 1.75M | 17 | 82.00% | 0.804 | 99.304% | 0.03096 | 17.30 | 2.08 min |\n",
        "| baseline | 6.98M | 17 | 83.84% | 0.880 | 99.960% | 0.00320 | 16.12 | 4.31 min |\n",
        "| w1.5 | 15.69M | 19 | 84.54% | 0.883 | 99.996% | 0.00082 | 15.46 | 7.94 min |\n",
        "| l2=1e-4 | 6.98M | 16 | 84.12% | 0.785 | 99.900% | 0.00727 | 15.78 | 4.40 min |\n",
        "| l2=1e-3 | 6.98M | 18 | 84.24% | 0.580 | 99.156% | 0.04136 | 14.92 | 4.19 min |\n",
        "| dropout=0 | 6.98M | 15 | 82.78% | 1.209 | 100.000% | 0.00051 | 17.22 | 4.08 min |\n",
        "| dropout=0.25 | 6.98M | 16 | 83.36% | 0.992 | 99.998% | 0.00128 | 16.64 | 4.09 min |\n",
        "\n",
        "**Capacity.** Halving width reduces wall time to 2.08 min and lowers validation accuracy to 82.00%. The smaller model still reaches 99.30% on clean training images, with a 17.30-point validation gap. This supports overfitting even at half width. Widening to 1.5x adds about 2.25x the parameters and 1.84x the wall time for +0.70 percentage points of validation accuracy. For all three widths, validation loss rises late in training as the training loss continues to fall.\n",
        "\n",
        "**L2.** Both weight decay settings improve validation accuracy over the baseline. At `l2=1e-3`, validation loss falls from 0.880 to 0.580 and the accuracy gap narrows from 16.12 to 14.92 points. The regularized model still fits the training data well (99.16%), with similar wall time to the baseline.\n",
        "\n",
        "**Dropout.** Removing head dropout increases the selected checkpoint's validation loss to 1.209 and the accuracy gap to 17.22 points. Dropout at 0.25 gives intermediate results, while 0.5 gives the highest validation accuracy in this comparison.\n",
        "\n",
        "The best validation accuracies differ by less than one percentage point among the baseline, both weight decay settings, and the wider model. The measurements come from one seed on a fixed split.\n"
      ]
