   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Now let's create the class that will apply the transformations\n",
    "from torch.utils.data import Dataset\n",
    "from torchvision import transforms\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "class AugmentedImages(Dataset):\n",
    "    def __init__(self, base_dataset):\n",
    "        self.base_dataset = base_dataset\n",
    "\n",
    "        # crop adds 4 pixels of padding around the image and then selects a 32x32 cell\n",
    "        self.transform = transforms.Compose([\n",
    "            transforms.RandomCrop(\n",
    "                size=32,\n",
    "                padding=4,\n",
    "                padding_mode=\"reflect\",\n",
    "            ),\n",
    "            transforms.RandomHorizontalFlip(p=0.5), # horizontal flip applies a mirror of the image left to right with probability p\n",
    "        ])\n",
    "\n",
    "    def __len__(self):\n",
    "        return len(self.base_dataset)\n",
    "\n",
    "    def __getitem__(self, index):\n",
    "        # apply the transformation\n",
    "        image, target, image_id = self.base_dataset[index]\n",
    "        augmented_image = self.transform(image)\n",
    "        return augmented_image, target, image_id\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## WHy this particular augmentation choice\n",
    "We decided to apply two transformations to the training images:\n",
    "\n",
    "- **Random crop with four pixels of reflection padding:** the image is\n",
    "  padded and a random crop of 32x32 pixels is selected. \n",
    "  This introduces small changes the object position within the image, forcing the model to recognize\n",
    "  objects without relying on their location in the image.\n",
    "\n",
    "- **Random horizontal flip with probability 0.5:** the image is mirrored\n",
    "  left-to-right. CIFAR-10 categories remain unchanged when an\n",
    "  element faces the opposite direction, so this helps the model to learn to \n",
    "  recognize both orientations.\n",
    "\n",
    "These transformations are applied randomly during training, before\n",
    "normalization. Validation images remain unchanged. \n",
    "Robustness is then measured separately using fixed, reproducible evaluation corruptions shared by both models.\n",
    "\n",
    "The transformations are deliberately moderate because we thought aggressive cropping might remove important\n",
    "parts of the elements inside the image and make the label ambiguous."
   ]
  },
